  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DEC Phase 1 - Inclusive humanitarian response to meet the urgent needs of flood affected populations of Sindh, Balochistan, Punjab and Khyber Pakhtunkhwa Provinces, Pakistan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed humanitarian response aims to provide immediate lifesaving support to highly vulnerable older people, older people&#x2019;s families, and persons with disabilities of all ages. 

This will be achieved through the following three outcomes:

Outcome A - Most vulnerable and marginalised flood-affected men, and women of all ages, boys, and girls, with and without disabilities, are identified and supported to access their basic survival needs

Outcome B &#x2013; Most vulnerable flood affected older people, people with disabilities and their families are identified and have better access to multipurpose cash grants

Outcome C - Humanitarian actors responding to emergencies have increased capacity to facilitate greater inclusion of older people and people with disabilities in their responses</narrative>
  </description>
